[59.409732, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe index is reachable. Now I’ll install version 0.1.0 using the exact `pip` command from the issue and verify the required import and behavior from a directory\r\nthat cannot shadow the installed package.\r\n\r\n```\r\npython3 -m pip uninstall -y vectorops >/dev/null 2>&1 || true\r\npip install --index-url http://localhost:8080/simple vectorops==0.1.0\r\ncd /tmp && python3 - <<'EOF'\r\nimport vectorops\r\nfrom vectorops import dotproduct\r\n\r\nassert vectorops.__version__ == \"0.1.0\"\r\nassert 1 == dotproduct([1, 1], [0, 1])\r\nassert 32 == dotproduct([1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6])\r\nassert 0 == dotproduct([], [])\r\nassert -2.5 == dotproduct([1.0, -2.0], [-0.5, 1.0])\r\ntry:\r\n    dotproduct([1], [1, 2])\r\nexcept ValueError:\r\n    pass\r\nelse:\r\n    raise AssertionError(\"length mismatch should raise ValueError\")\r\nprint(\"Installed version:\", vectorops.__version__)\r\nprint(\"Package file:\", vectorops.__file__)\r\nprint(\"dotproduct checks passed\")\r\nEOF\r\npython3 -m pip show vectorops\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠼\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[59.410109, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠼\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
